# `core.autocrlf` is on for Windows checkouts, and a shell script it rewrote is one a Linux container
# reads a carriage return off the end of every line of. These are bind-mounted into containers as the
# working copy holds them, so the working copy has to hold LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Its `deps` command is a shell script in a block scalar, which `sh -c` reads the same way.
compose.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
